  "worked_solution": "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x(\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x+2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x+\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
